              19,
              17,
              6,
              25
            ],
            "decimals": 0,
            "label": "Turn-taking gap",
            "note": "The silence between one person finishing and the other starting. Get this wrong in a voice model and it either interrupts the user or leaves them hanging.\n\nWe merge the voiced stretches of both tracks onto one timeline. Every change of speaker gives one gap, and the figure is the median of them. Where the next speaker started early the two are talking at once, so that goes under Overlap instead.\n\nCANDOR, a large public corpus of natural conversation, reports 380 milliseconds. It ships as `turn_taking_gap_ms`.",
            "p5": 280,
            "p50": 580,
            "p95": 1120,
            "unit": "ms"
          },
          {
            "binMax": 0.87,
            "binMin": 0.16,
