            ],
            "decimals": 2,
            "label": "Speech dominance",
            "note": "Speaker A’s share of the talking, where 0.5 is an even split.\n\nWe count the 20 millisecond frames in which A is voiced, then divide by the frames in which either speaker is. Overlapping speech counts for both people, so the two shares add up to more than 1 when they talk at once.\n\nThe metadata field `speech_dominance` is a different number. That one is A’s share of the transcript words.",
            "p5": 0.27,
            "p50": 0.56,
            "p95": 0.81,
            "unit": "share"
          },
          {
            "binMax": 234,
