              41,
              54
            ],
            "decimals": 0,
            "label": "Speaking rate",
            "note": "How fast a person speaks, in words per minute of actual speaking time.\n\nThe denominator is the choice that matters, so we tested three across 28 channels of real conversation. Dividing by the whole recording gave 74 words per minute at the median. That measures how much of the call each person held, not how fast they talk. Voice activity detection gave 192, but it counts breaths, laughter and a partner’s bleed as talking, and it swung from 82 to 281 on the same audio.\n\nSo we sum each word’s own duration from the transcript and divide the word count by that. Only entries typed as words count, on both sides of the division. It ships as `avg_wpm`.",
            "p5": 156,
            "p50": 186,
            "p95": 218,
            "unit": "words/min"
          }
        ],
